---
description: Voice pipeline rules for Anchor and Caller
globs: app/anchor/**, app/caller/**, app/producer/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Voice runs on Pipecat. Keep STT, TTS and transport behind small adapters (`adapters/deepgram.py`, `adapters/cartesia.py`) so providers can be swapped by config.
- Anchor only accepts script lines whose claims are all approved and cleared by Standards Desk. Enforce this in code, not by convention.
- Stream TTS sentence by sentence. Record `audio_start_ms` and `audio_end_ms` per script line for transcript sync.
- Barge-in: when Caller detects speech, Anchor pauses within 300 ms and the Producer decides to answer or resume.
- Track a latency budget per Caller stage (stt, intent, search, write, judge, first_audio) and emit each as an Archive span.
- Never block the audio loop on network calls. Use queues between pipeline stages.
